---
# clang-tidy configuration (#123).
#
# The code-quality job runs clang-tidy over the tree (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
# Before this file existed it ran with clang-tidy's defaults, and because that step
# reports rather than fails, findings were visible but never remembered. This file
# fixes *what* is looked for; it does not make the step fail - that is a separate
# decision (the determinism document lists it as kept-by-review for exactly that
# reason).
#
# The check list is deliberately small: whole categories are enabled, the noisy
# members of those categories are disabled by name. There is no naming or style
# policy here on purpose - inventing one in a config file would be a review rule
# pretending to be a check. Use clang-format (already enforced) for formatting.
Checks: >
  clang-diagnostic-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -clang-analyzer-alpha.*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -performance-inefficient-string-concatenation
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
FormatStyle: none
